CYBERGRAM — IDEAS (updated 2026-10-02)

This is the owner's original idea list, updated with every decision made
since. The binding details live in the design docs (design/gdd/*.md); the
"Canon" table in design/gdd/game-concept.md wins if anything here disagrees.
The original notes are in git history (commit 300baf5).

Mode: PvP, 5v5, first person. Bots fill empty slots and replace disconnects.
    A co-op mode against bots (PvE) can come later; the bots are needed anyway.

Style:
    Design: Anime/Cartoon, cel-shaded (see design/art-bible.md)
    Theme: Futuristic Fantasy
    World: Halcyra. Teams: Azure Concord (blue) vs Ember Syndicate (red).

Weapons:
    Main: one signature gun per hero, Mana-based or Mechanical
    Upgrades: bought in-match only (no pay-to-win, nothing carries over)
        Visible on the gun: every gun has Core, Barrel and Frame sockets.
        Mana guns take Crystals, Mechanical guns take Chips, each in 3 tiers.
        Each mount changes the gun's model, glow and sound.
    Ammo: 6 ammo types (Piercing, Incendiary, Shock, Siphon, Cryo, Sunder)
        that go in a 4th "Chamber" socket, plus 5 ammo mods that change
        how they behave.

Characters: Heroes like LoL/Dota with 4 skills, upgraded during the match.
    Types: Mana and Mechanical (4 Mana heroes, 3 Mechanical)
    Mana: gun fires from a recharging pool; emptying it causes "Burnout"
    Mechanical: magazines + reserve ammo, refilled at the Armory, Supply
        Caches and from enemy Wardling drops
    Skills use cooldowns for every hero; the type only affects the gun.

Maps:
    War-like front line. One map, 3 lanes, 5 hardpoints per lane (15 total).
    Each hardpoint is a task: Hold (outnumber in the zone), Plant (carry a
    Mana Cell in and defend it), or Breach (destroy a shield generator).
    You can only attack the next hardpoint along your lane, so the front
    moves step by step toward the enemy HQ.
    First playable map: "Shardline Causeway", 1 lane, 5 hardpoints.

Mobs = "Wardlings":
    Personal squad: 3 free at your HQ Foundry when you spawn, buy up to 5.
        Variants to buy: Shieldling, Striker, Seeker, Mender, Sapper.
        They follow you and help defend more than attack (middle-ground
        strength: a base squad does ~30% of the Soldier's damage).
        4 commands: Follow, Hold Here, Attack Target, Go Capture.
        If you die they hold position 10 s, then dissolve.
    Vanguard waves: every 60 s each team sends 4 Wardlings per lane to
        the front. Small, capped, objective-driven; no last-hitting.
    Money (Lumen) comes mainly from killing enemy Wardlings, shared by
        everyone nearby.

Skills:
    Minimal skill tree per skill: Unlock -> Boost -> Fork (pick A or B)
        -> Mastery (level 9+)
    4 fixed skills per hero (3 basic + 1 ultimate with 3 ranks)
    Skill points from EXP ("Resonance"); level cap 15 = everything unlocked

UI/UX (see design/ux/hud.md):
    Front-line bar and objective strip showing who holds each hardpoint
    Health and Mana bar, or magazine + reserve
    Squad strip showing each Wardling's health and current command
    Minimap and tactical map with the front line and Uplink state

EXP ("Resonance"):
    Killing Wardlings, killing heroes and assists, capturing and defending
    hardpoints. Killing a higher-level hero pays a catch-up bonus.

Heroes:
1. Vesper Loom - Minionmancer: controls and empowers Wardlings; her ult
   upgrades them and can take over enemy waves.
2. Sable - Infiltrator: phases through Barricades, plants sabotage charges.
3. Juniper Quill - Trapper: chainable snares, tripwires and mines.
4. Ryker Vance - Soldier: highest damage, no big defensive ability.
5. Brannoc - Tank: lots of HP, shield wall, short-range heavy weapon.
6. Liora Vale - Healer: heals with her gun's mana alt-fire and Med-Packs.
7. Hex - Hacker: makes enemy traps, turrets, Barricades and Wardlings
   malfunction.

Rounds:
    Duration: max 60 min; target 25-35 min. The match escalates at 15:00
        and 30:00 (Surges) and at 45:00 (Mana Drought).
    Win: destroy the enemy "Mana Uplink" (33,000 Integrity). It can only
        be damaged once you hold one of the enemy's Inner hardpoints, and
        damage never heals.
    At 60:00: the team further into the enemy side wins (points per lane);
        if equal, whoever did more damage to the enemy Uplink wins.
    Tie: Sudden Death at the Mid Plaza until one team is the last on the
        map. If the last two fighters kill each other, it resets and starts
        again (after 3 resets the next round is final; see
        design/open-questions.md).

Mana Uplink:
    Broadcasts "the Cybergram", the signal that lets normal humans use
    mana and magic. Destroyed = that team can no longer use mana and loses.
